# Normalise line endings and mark source as text.
#
# Added after worker/admin.js was committed with a literal NUL byte in a regex
# character class, which made git classify it as binary -- so diffs, blame and
# code review were silently useless for that file. The content is fixed, but
# `* text=auto` plus explicit rules make the intent unambiguous and stop git
# guessing from content alone.
#
# This does NOT override git's NUL-based binary detection; it removes the
# line-ending ambiguity that leads to the same class of surprise. The check that
# actually catches literal control bytes is in assets/app.test.mjs.

* text=auto

*.js   text
*.mjs  text
*.css  text
*.html text
*.py   text
*.yml  text
*.toml text
*.md   text
*.json text

# Generated feed data: large, machine-written, and committed as-is.
data/*.json text -diff

# Binary-ish assets, if any are ever added.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.ico  binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
